From eedf06c187a23545eff5522f66861ce28374b17b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: C0fuge <189659128+C0fuge@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:50:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libhdfs3: Record and log the negotiated data-transfer QOP / cipher per
 DataNode

The negotiated data-transfer protection was only logged at DEBUG1, and
libhdfs3 prints nothing at all unless HDFS_ENABLE_LOGGING=true, so a
caller could not tell auth from auth-conf or 3des from AES.

- TransferInfo: process-wide record per DataNode (host(ip):xferPort) of
  the last negotiated qop ("none" for plain connections without SASL),
  cipher, AES key bits, new connections, failed handshakes, last error
  (bounded to 10000 DataNodes).
- Each new SASL connection logs "DataTransferSasl: DataNode <dn>: qop
  <qop>, cipher <cipher>" (AES: "cipher option AES/CTR/NoPadding, key
  <n> bits") at INFO; the first one per DataNode and any change is
  written even without HDFS_ENABLE_LOGGING=true (LOG_ALWAYS, still
  subject to dfs.client.log.severity), further ones through the normal
  gated log.
- C API hdfsGetDataTransferInfo / hdfsFreeDataTransferInfo.
